{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And it shall rise</b> — the essence of the day is the sun, as in 'the heat of the day the sun' and 'the sun declined greatly,' and likewise the coming day. And this sun will not harm the people of HaShem, only heal." "<b>With its wings</b> — the light that goes forth from the sun, spread over the face of the earth, like wings." "<b>And you shall go forth</b> — to the light of the sun." "<b>And you shall trample</b> — I have explained it [elsewhere]."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:23.555816075Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}